WEBVTT

00:36:29.363 --> 00:36:32.307
for whom it's a very
deliberate strategy, right?

00:36:32.331 --> 00:36:37.126
They'll say, "Look, I believe the world
is a dog-eat-dog competitive place,

00:36:37.150 --> 00:36:40.226
and I have to put myself first
because no one else will,

00:36:40.250 --> 00:36:43.246
and that's how I get ahead,
that's how I win."

00:36:43.635 --> 00:36:45.409
And on the other end of the spectrum,

00:36:45.433 --> 00:36:46.615
you have people who,

00:36:46.639 --> 00:36:49.313
it's almost like they're in the movie
"The Sixth Sense."

00:36:49.703 --> 00:36:52.185
Everybody else knows they're a taker,

00:36:52.209 --> 00:36:54.421
but they have no idea.

00:36:54.445 --> 00:36:58.846
And I think the Richard Feynman quote

00:36:58.870 --> 00:37:00.463
always stands out here, that,